WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:23.095
"It's a nice day for a hike," said Dad.

2
00:00:23.096 --> 00:00:27.753
"Yeah," said Oliver.

3
00:00:27.754 --> 00:00:32.603
"I want to hike to the top of a mountain!"

4
00:00:32.604 --> 00:00:39.689
"Hiking up a mountain is hard," said Mom.

5
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:47.735
"I can do it!" said Oliver.

6
00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:53.393
Dad drove the car to the mountain.

7
00:00:53.394 --> 00:01:00.197
Everybody put on backpacks.

8
00:01:00.198 --> 00:01:04.190
"I can carry the bottles of water," said Harry.

9
00:01:04.191 --> 00:01:08.478
"I can carry the apples," said Emmy.

10
00:01:08.479 --> 00:01:12.837
"I can carry the first aid kit," said Mom.

11
00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:16.612
"I can carry the map," said Oliver.

12
00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:20.608
Dad laughed.

13
00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:24.144
"I have nothing to carry!" he said.

14
00:01:24.145 --> 00:01:27.636
Everybody hiked on the trail.

15
00:01:27.637 --> 00:01:33.671
The trail went up.

16
00:01:33.672 --> 00:01:37.981
"Are you tired?" Mom asked Oliver.

17
00:01:37.982 --> 00:01:40.848
"Nope," said Oliver.

18
00:01:40.849 --> 00:01:44.444
"This is easy!"

19
00:01:44.445 --> 00:01:48.234
The family hiked some more.

20
00:01:48.235 --> 00:01:54.258
Oliver huffed and puffed.

21
00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:58.438
"Are you tired?" asked Emmy.

22
00:01:58.439 --> 00:02:03.445
"Just a little bit," said Oliver.

23
00:02:03.446 --> 00:02:07.368
The trail got very steep.

24
00:02:07.369 --> 00:02:11.353
Oliver started to walk slowly.

25
00:02:11.354 --> 00:02:14.586
"Are you tired?" asked Harry.

26
00:02:14.587 --> 00:02:19.785
"I can make it," said Oliver.

27
00:02:19.786 --> 00:02:27.020
At last the trail stopped.

28
00:02:27.021 --> 00:02:32.061
"We are at the top," said Dad.

29
00:02:32.062 --> 00:02:41.313
"I made it!" said Oliver.

30
00:02:41.314 --> 00:02:46.107
"Now we hike down the mountain," said Mom.

31
00:02:46.108 --> 00:02:49.035
Oliver sat down.

32
00:02:49.036 --> 00:02:54.284
"I'm too tired," said Oliver.

33
00:02:54.285 --> 00:03:00.340
"Now I have something to carry," said Dad.

34
00:03:00.341 --> 00:03:07.468
"I can carry Oliver!"
